---
description: RSNA Knee Kaggle preprocessing and local GPU workflow
alwaysApply: true
---

- Follow AGENTS.md and read PROJECT.md before work.
- The main terminal is a Windows desktop with RTX 4090. Build image caches on Kaggle, train locally from caches, and run submission inference on Kaggle.
- Do not download the entire raw MRI dataset locally. Workflow preparation does not start competition data/model acquisition, real MRI decoding or training.
- Keep Report out of inference inputs; share preprocessing between training and prediction.
- Preserve missing labels and the official-label holdout. Never select checkpoints on gold.
- Record evidence, source versions, config, fold, seed and runtime for experiments.
- Keep data, reports, caches, weights and credentials outside Git.
- Update project status without claiming unrun training or Kaggle reproduction succeeded.
